      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "34CD8qcoslK9rvh15tuuX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 124.36617260351954,
      "y": 1050.507852125371,
      "width": 1214.33935546875,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 977911147,
      "version": 1273,
      "versionNonce": 1502217035,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787338772232,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "a) At the start of the level the building will be constructed the same way as now: a matrix will iterate until the desired\ncolumns and rows of blocks is available.\nb) We will create a BuildingArea: a rectangle of the same size of the building. It will work as sensor\nc) The ContactListener will listen when a block exits or enter in it and somehow we will count the rows of the building that\nhave not been demolished.\nd) The Level will have a 'buildingHeightTarget' property which represents the desired height of the building. i.e.: our building\nis 8 floors height, but we desire it to be 1. Then we must throw all the above floors (block-rows) and we win when we reach\nthat height.\ne) Level have 'availableShots' which represent the quantity of shoots we have (activated with spacebar)\nf) If we use all our available shots, or reach the buildingHeightTarget the game ends",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "a) At the start of the level the building will be constructed the same way as now: a matrix will iterate until the desired\ncolumns and rows of blocks is available.\nb) We will create a BuildingArea: a rectangle of the same size of the building. It will work as sensor\nc) The ContactListener will listen when a block exits or enter in it and somehow we will count the rows of the building that\nhave not been demolished.\nd) The Level will have a 'buildingHeightTarget' property which represents the desired height of the building. i.e.: our building\nis 8 floors height, but we desire it to be 1. Then we must throw all the above floors (block-rows) and we win when we reach\nthat height.\ne) Level have 'availableShots' which represent the quantity of shoots we have (activated with spacebar)\nf) If we use all our available shots, or reach the buildingHeightTarget the game ends",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
